.TH HD-MENU 1 "October 2026" "hd-desktop" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-menu \- a menu for the HyprDebian desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-menu
.RI < menu.json
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-menu
shows a menu in the middle of the screen, chosen from with the keyboard,
and prints the value of the option chosen on stdout.
It takes no arguments; it reads the menu as JSON from stdin.
.PP
It draws on a wlr-layer-shell surface over the whole output, so it needs a
Wayland compositor with wlr-layer-shell, such as Hyprland.
The menu has the keyboard to itself while it is open.
Only one
.B hd-menu
is open at a time: another one exits at once with 1.
.SH THE MENU
.nf
{
    "banner": "Reboot system?",
    "width": 500,
    "options": [
        {"label": "No", "default": true},
        {"label": "Yes", "value": "yes", "icon": "/usr/share/icons/reboot.svg"}
    ]
}
.fi
.TP
.B banner
Optional: a line of text at the top of the menu.
.TP
.B width
Optional: the width of the menu, in logical pixels (a number) or as a
percentage of the output (a string such as \(dq50%\(dq).
Without it, the menu is just wide enough for the banner and the options.
.TP
.B height
Optional: the height of the menu, likewise.
Without it, the menu is just high enough for the banner and all options.
.TP
.B options
The options, in this order; at least one.
Each is an object with:
.RS
.TP
.B label
The text shown.
.TP
.B value
Optional: what
.B hd-menu
prints when the option is chosen; the label when there is none.
.TP
.B icon
Optional: the path of a PNG or SVG
.RB ( .svg " or " .svgz )
image, shown left of the label at the
.B icon_size
of the theme.
An icon that cannot be loaded is left out, with a message on stderr.
.TP
.B default
Optional: true for the option selected at the start; the first option when
none has it.
.RE
.PP
Other members are ignored.
The menu is never larger than the output; options that do not fit scroll.
.PP
The Font Awesome glyphs of the Nerd Font of
.BR hd-fonts ,
such as \e\&uf00c (a check mark) and \e\&uf00d (a cross), can be written as
escapes in a label.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR Up ", " Down ", " Tab
Select the previous or next option.
.TP
.BR "Page Up" ", " "Page Down" ", " Home ", " End
Move a page, or to the first or the last option.
.TP
.B Enter
Choose the selected option.
.TP
.BR Escape ", " q
Close the menu without a choice. q is the key with the letter q in the
keyboard layout, with or without Shift.
.PP
A key that is held repeats at the rate and after the delay of the compositor,
.B input:repeat_rate
and
.B input:repeat_delay
in Hyprland, so that holding Down keeps moving the selection.
.SH THE THEME
.B hd-menu
draws the menu in the
.B hd-theme
of the configuration of the user,
.IR ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json ,
or, when that has none, of the configuration of the system,
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ;
when neither has it, it uses defaults of its own, and run as root it only
reads the configuration of the system.
.BR hd-theme (1)
sets the key when a theme is selected.
The theme gives the font and its
.BR font-size-big ,
the colours
.B dark
(the background, at
.BR opacity ),
.B light
(the text),
.B normal
(the selected option and the divider) and
.B highlight
(the border), the
.B border
width, the corner
.B radius
and the
.BR icon_size .
The font size is in points, like in the other programs of the theme;
.B hd-menu
draws it at 4/3 logical pixels per point.
The border, the radius and the icon size are in logical pixels.
The scale of the monitor decides how large that is on the screen, so the
menu has the same size as the other programs on every monitor.
A setting that is missing has its default; when the file cannot be read, the
whole theme has.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
An option was chosen; its value is on stdout.
.TP
.B 1
The menu was closed without a choice, or another
.B hd-menu
is open.
.TP
.B 2
An error: arguments, invalid JSON on stdin, a menu without options, or no
Wayland compositor with wlr-layer-shell.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json
The theme of the user, in
.BR hd-theme .
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The theme of the system, in
.BR hd-theme ,
when the user has none.
.TP
.IR /run/user/ UID /hd-menu.lock
The lock that keeps a second
.B hd-menu
from opening.
.SH EXAMPLES
Ask before a reboot:
.PP
.nf
choice=$(echo \(aq{"banner": "Reboot system?", "options": [{"label": "No"}, {"label": "Yes"}]}\(aq | hd-menu)
if [[ "$choice" == "Yes" ]]; then
    hd-reboot
fi
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-desktop (7),
.BR hd-theme (1),
.BR hd-config (7),
.BR hd-reboot (1)
